buffer_cache: EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY=1 sizes native compute bindings from the mapping only in DLSS

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine 8820bb79aa (rdenno, PR #571, on nx2 since 2026-11-05), in the form of
PR #609 (Mcm190) and viejunerd/Eglantine-PS5- core patch 0047: every native binding keeps the
device-contiguity clamp. GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

Sizing every native compute binding from its mapping binds up to 8 MiB per buffer. The upstream
reports: Hyrule Warriors' fights fall to a few fps, then hang (8820bb79aa); Mario Kart World 1.8.0
reads back several GiB/s (#609). Our tree still does it.

With the switch only passes of a game DLSS evaluation, and table pointers (0170's indirect_offset),
size from the mapping. Other native compute bindings go back to the word after the pointer when it
looks like a size, else up to 8 MiB. Graphics bindings are unchanged.

Changed from the source: off unless EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY=1; table pointers stay mapping-sized,
which 0170 needs and the source does not have. A member set for the length of
BindComputeStorageBuffer carries the choice, not a new argument, so this does not touch the lines
fog-03 changes. #609's VI2 pacing half (#547) is left out: it only acts once Mario Kart World's
dynamic FPS patch applies.

Risk: Ocarina of Time's culling reads may want the whole mapping. Try it on Mario Kart World first.

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 2d78b98a5c..1faecbae0a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -812,6 +812,18 @@ void BufferCache<P>::UnbindComputeStorageBuffers() {
 template <class P>
 void BufferCache<P>::BindComputeStorageBuffer(size_t ssbo_index, u32 cbuf_index, u32 cbuf_offset,
                                               bool is_written, u32 indirect_offset) {
+    // EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY=1: only DLSS passes size a native compute binding from the mapping.
+    // Doing it for every native dispatch binds up to 8 MiB per buffer: Hyrule Warriors' fights fell
+    // to a few fps, and Mario Kart World read back several GiB/s (upstream 8820bb79aa, PR #609).
+    static const bool dlss_only = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    compute_binding_sized_by_descriptor =
+        dlss_only && indirect_offset == ~0U && !kepler_compute->IsDlssDispatch();
+    SCOPE_EXIT {
+        compute_binding_sized_by_descriptor = false;
+    };
     if (ssbo_index >= channel_state->compute_storage_buffers.size()) [[unlikely]] {
         LOG_ERROR(HW_GPU, "Storage buffer index {} exceeds maximum storage buffer count",
                   ssbo_index);
@@ -3144,7 +3156,7 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
         // A native (Switch 2) compute program's pointer is bare: the word after it is another
         // parameter (a dimension, stride or texture handle), not an NVN buffer size. Taking it as
         // one bound Fortune's Weave's DLSS input features to 266 bytes and dropped the rest.
-        if (native_pointer) {
+        if (native_pointer && !compute_binding_sized_by_descriptor) {
             return (std::min)(memory_layout_size, static_cast<u32>(8_MiB));
         }
         const u64 next_qword = gpu_memory->Read<u64>(ssbo_addr + 8);
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
index 8b82c5b0c0..c40b96ac96 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
@@ -774,6 +774,9 @@ private:
     Common::RangeSet<DAddr> cpu_read_ranges;
     bool download_cpu_read_ranges{};
     Common::RangeSet<DAddr> gpu_modified_ranges;
+    /// The compute binding being made takes its size from the word after its pointer, if that
+    /// looks like a size (EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY=1).
+    bool compute_binding_sized_by_descriptor{};
     std::deque<Common::RangeSet<DAddr>> committed_gpu_modified_ranges;
 
     // Async Buffers
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
index fa5c91adb4..6cafb47887 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
@@ -244,6 +244,8 @@ public:
     }
 
     bool IsNativeMode() const { return native_mode; }
+    /// Whether the dispatch being run is a pass of a game DLSS evaluation (Fortune's Weave).
+    bool IsDlssDispatch() const { return native_mode && dlss_chain.active; }
     /// Whether the matrix multiplies (tensor-core instructions) of the program being dispatched
     /// are emulated: in a game DLSS evaluation when the game's own network may draw, and always
